	(footprint "Mylib:TYPE-C-16P-CB1.6"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "b623cf57-4307-4fbd-8cd4-6455079a7c45")
		(at 100 130.32 180)
		(descr "USB 2.0 Type-C receptacle, 16P, mid-mount (JLCPCB calls it 'laminated board'), for a 1.6mm board: SHOU HAN TYPE-C 16P CB1.6 073, LCSC C2906290.  The body drops into a 9.24 x 6.50mm notch in the board edge, so the Edge.Cuts here is real geometry and the board outline has to be broken to meet it.  Contact row is the datasheet's recommended layout and agrees with EasyEDA's own C2906290 to 0um.  Two places it does not: the notch, which EasyEDA draws 9.00mm wide and off centre - narrower than the 8.94mm body on one side - so this uses the datasheet's 9.24 centred; and the shell holes, where the recommended layout gives 1.80 near the edge and 0.80 behind it.  0.80 is the far pin, not its hole: the side view draws a 1.20 pin in a 1.80 hole and a 0.80 pin in a 1.20 hole, so the far holes here are 0.60 x 1.20.")
		(tags "USB C Type-C receptacle mid-mount midmount laminated 16P USB2.0 SHOU HAN CB1.6 C2906290")
